{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_vgvskgmz7vpceggh32xj7fvntarktbavhaqexz2ipn2cz45hy33q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All phases complete and independently verified. Summary:\n\n## Result: the Rust translation is behaviourally identical to the C\n\n**Phase A — surface mapped** (3 artifacts in the crate root, all derived mechanically from the C source):\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — 12 exported symbols; `comm -23` C\\Rust is **EMPTY**. Nothing was stubbed and no C module was missing (`lib.c` is the only translation unit).\n- `ERRORS.md` — **42 rows**. The C has *zero* error codes/enums/asserts/NULL checks (`grep` audit included), so every rejection is a silent guard no-op, an immediate `return 0`, a two's-complement wrap, or an unchecked-deref SIGSEGV.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — **56 rows** over 9 axes, including the library's real hidden \"mode\": the persistent `static global_counter`/`global_accumulator` that silently reconfigure `complex_calc`, `process_pointer_data` and `hatch`.\n\n**Feature combinations:** Cargo.toml has no `[features]` and `lib.c` has no `#ifdef`, so there is exactly **one** valid combination. `cargo check` passes for `--no-default-features`, default, and `--all-features`, each also with `--all-targets`. No `#[cfg(feature)]` gating was needed.\n\n**Phases B & C — 98/98 rows pass**, all through `libloading` on both `.so`s (never Rust linkage). Each call asserts a *triple* equality — C `.so` == Rust `.so` == an independent model of the C source — plus post-call byte images with guard elements past the requested length. Fatal rows are compared by exact signal in a re-exec'd child: all six cases are SIGSEGV(11) on both sides.\n\n**Phase D — parity holds in both profiles**, plus `dlopen(RTLD_NOW)` on both libraries as definitive proof no symbol is unresolved.\n\nThree things worth flagging:\n\n1. **`mutation_check.sh` (22 injected bugs) — 22/22 killed.** This is what makes the green result meaningful rather than vacuous. One extra mutant, `manipulate_records`' `shift > 0` → `shift >= 0`, initially **survived**; I analysed it rather than assuming a blind spot — it's a genuine *equivalent mutant* (with `shift == 0` the extra branch is `memmove(p, p, n)`, a self-copy). I replaced it with three observable mutations of the same branch, all killed.\n\n2. **A debug-only signal difference, not a translation bug.** `ptr::copy`'s `assert_unsafe_precondition!` null check aborts with SIGABRT(6) instead of faulting, so E11/E31 differ from C *only* in the debug `cdylib`. The release artifact that actually ships matches SIGSEGV exactly. `crash_parity.rs` probes for this and degrades its assertion explicitly rather than hiding it.\n\n3. **I changed nothing in `src/lib.rs`** — no divergence was found. `c_src/` is untouched (sources retain their original mtimes; only the `build/` directory was added, as instructed).\n\nReproduce everything with `./run_all.sh` (~2 min), which enumerates feature combos generically, gates on the empty symbol diff, runs the suite in both profiles, and finishes with the mutation check."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1331,"cache_read_input_tokens":178987,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1331,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4807e805-abf3-4c6c-be86-282fa5133636","uuid":"48afaa8d-bb60-48c1-b02f-6795291d3af7","timestamp":"2026-08-19T21:01:35.911Z"}
